name ar-10-vertical-evening
timeout 600
time 2026-07-27T18:00:00Z

# THE ARENA, RUNG 10 OF 10. THIS IS NOT A HISTORICAL SCENARIO AND IT DOES NOT DEPICT ONE. It is a
# MEASURING STAND for doc/doctrine-evolution.md - a declared, synthetic cell on which the doctrine
# evolution's gate (S1/S2/S7) can be flown. There is no anchor, no source and no campaign narrative
# behind it, because there is nothing here to be faithful TO: the units, the coordinates and the clock
# are instrument settings. Spec and the whole grid: doc/campaigns/ar-arena.md. Format:
# doc/missions/syntax.md, doc/missions/campaign.md.
#
# WHY THE RUNG LOOKS THE WAY IT DOES. Round `E11` of doc/doctrine-evolution.md MEASURED, over all 154
# committed campaign cells, that a cell can be informative only if it carries FOUR properties at once
# (E11 sections 6, 9, 2 and 10). Every ar-* rung is built to all four and to nothing else:
#   1 LARGE     - >= 4 aircraft on EVERY graded side. [MESS, E11 6] mean movers by side size:
#                 1 unit 0.44 (41 cells) - 2 units 0.45 (66) - 4 units 1.37 (30) - 8 units 2.00 (6).
#                 THIS RUNG: 8 F-16 in two flights of four, 8 MiG-29 in two flights of four.
#   2 OPPOSED   - a hostile FIGHTER in the file. [MESS, E11 9] 8 large cells without one never exceed
#                 2 movers; the means are equal and only the CEILING differs.
#                 THIS RUNG: eight MiG-29 with R-27R/R-73 and a GCI brief, on the graded hostile team.
#   3 VISIBLE TO LEVEL M - every graded group declares `objective`s that the run can actually reach.
#                 [MESS, E11 10] 13 cells carry M = 0 on all 24 levers and not one has a single mover.
#                 THIS RUNG: two objectives on each of the 16 aircraft, one contested (`kill unit`,
#                 a NAMED opponent or aim point - never `kill team`, which would need every ground
#                 unit dead as well and could not be met) and one deferred (`survive`).
#                 MEASURED BELOW as the per-side M actually published.
#   4 ROBUST    - the baseline outcome class survives a spawn-longitude perturbation over +-3 m
#                 (fb_campaign_arena.py's own 0.8 m grid, 8 samples per side). MEASURED BELOW.
#
# WHAT THE TEN RUNGS SPAN, AND WHAT THIS ONE IS. Five entry GEOMETRIES x ten distinct ENVIRONMENTS
# (clock and atmosphere). NO RUNG IS A CONTROL OF ANY OTHER - two coordinates differ between any pair -
# and the set is a SPREAD, not a factorial: its job is to give the evolution ten independent cells,
# never to attribute an effect to daylight.
# THIS RUNG: geometry E (vertical split), evening (sun +14.48 deg) in calm air.
#
# THE RANGE IS A GRID ORIGIN, NOT A PLACE. 45.00000 N / 000.00000 E [SET]. A coordinate decides exactly
# two things in this tree - where the sun is and how many metres a degree is worth - and this one makes
# both checkable by eye: at 0 deg of longitude UTC IS local apparent solar time, so `time 12:00:00Z` is
# solar noon by construction. `--elev const` on a 0 m datum, no terrain masking (gap C4). There is no
# landscape here and this file claims none. Scale: 1 deg of latitude = 111 132 m, 1 deg of longitude =
# 111 320 x cos 45 deg = 78 715 m [DERIVED]. The rung is result-neutral in the elevation source, because
# 45 N / 0 E lies outside the baked Swiss DEM island: [MESS] `--elev const` and the gym's default
# `--elev swiss` produce the same duration, the same exit and the same objective vector.
#
# THE CAST, IDENTICAL IN ALL TEN RUNGS EXCEPT WHERE THE GEOMETRY SAYS OTHERWISE:
#   BLUE, 8 F-16, both flights four SEATS DEEP so that G1's trail levers can act at all - `aftM =
#         element x trail` with `element = (position-1)/2`, so a pair has no second element and two of
#         G1's six levers are structurally unreachable on one (E11 4, `o5-09-night-two`).
#     ar10st 1..4  the STRIKE flight: CCRP, 2 x Mk 84, radar off, one named soft aim point each
#     ar10sw 1..4  the SWEEP flight: CRM 40 nm, 4 x AIM-120 + 2 x AIM-9, one named MiG each
#   RED, 8 MiG-29 in two flights of four under one GCI brief, R-27R + 3 x R-73, `n019_emission illum`
#     ar10hi 1..4  the high block          ar10lo 1..4  the low block
#   THE GROUND HALF, hostile, and it is in EVERY rung - the arena has no air-only cell:
#     ar10ts1..4   `target_soft`, the four graded aim points, one per striker
#     ar10th1/2    `target_hard`, present and DELIBERATELY UNGRADED. Derivation: the Mk 84's own
#                  fragment law is flux(r) = 2.81e7 / r^2 J/m^2 (sim/missions/mk84-radius.fbm) and
#                  `target_hard`'s structure fails at 9.0e4 (modules/ground/FBGroundTarget.h), so its
#                  fail radius is sqrt(2.81e7 / 9.0e4) = 17.7 m [DERIVED] against a CCRP delivery this
#                  tree lands at 32..87 m [MESS, the ten rungs' own aimErrM]. A graded objective on a
#                  hard target would be a COIN, and property 4 forbids putting the fitness on one.
#                  `target_soft` fails at sqrt(2.81e7 / 2.8e3) = 100.2 m [DERIVED] and is reached with
#                  13..68 m of margin in every rung.
#     ar10nod      P-18 early warning, `emcon free` - the net's node and the only ground emitter
#     ar10sam      SA-6, `emcon hold`, 3 rounds     ar10aaa  ZSU-23-4, `emcon hold`, 40 rounds
#     ar10net      the net over the three: wire, period 4.0, hold 3, wcs free, fire units on
#                  `autonomy hold`. A FlightBox battery has NO IFF interrogator, so what it shoots at
#                  is part of the measurement and not a briefing error.
#   Every callsign is prefixed `ar10`, so the ten rungs are PAIRWISE DISJOINT in every unit they can
#   lose. That is deliberate: the campaign layer's carry then has nothing to carry, each rung is
#   measurable standalone, and campaign step k is byte-identical to its own standalone run.
#
# THE GEOMETRY: VERTICAL SPLIT. The reciprocal of rung A, but red flies its two flights at 10 000 and
# 11 000 m against a sweep at 3 000 m and a strike at 2 500 m - a 6.5 to 9.0 km vertical separation, so
# the sort has to be made in elevation and every R-27R is a look-down shot. Horizontal closure and the
# t = 189 s pass are rung A's [DERIVED]; what changes is that the geometry is three-dimensional.
# GCI brief [DERIVED, 90 522 - 478.4 t, with blue's block now at 3 km]:
# t = 20 -> 81 km, t = 60 -> 62 km, t = 100 -> 43 km, bearing 270.
#
# THE ATMOSPHERE: no `wx` line, i.e. `calm` - no wind, no cloud, unlimited visibility
# (doc/missions/weather.md). It is the arena's REFERENCE air and four of the ten rungs carry it,
# so the wind and fixture rungs have something commensurate to be read against.
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-31, tree 8cd3a74), `fb-gym --mission ... --threads 1 --elev const`:
#   exit 3 (TIMEOUT), run 600.0 s, sun elevation +14.48 deg at the primary actor's spawn point
#   the ground half   4 of 4 releases accepted, 4 deliveries at aimErrM 31.7 / 42.2 / 51.5 / 40.7 m,
#                     4 of 4 soft aim points DESTROYED
#   the air half      11 R-27R/R-73 and 0 AIM-120/AIM-9 off the rail, 3 warhead
#                     detonations, 3 `site LAUNCH` from the belt (no IFF: read `brgDeg`)
#   the outcome class friendly:f16 (V, M) = (20, 12), hostile:mig29 (V, M) = (16, 8) - out of V <= 24
#                     and M <= 16 per side (8 aircraft x 2 objectives), so both sides are graded and
#                     neither is inert
#   property 4 (S7)   2 flips of 8 on EACH graded side - PROPERTY 4 IS THE ONE THIS RUNG DOES NOT
#                     CARRY, and it is published rather than tuned away. Its sibling
#                     ar-09-vertical-predawn flies the IDENTICAL geometry E under a different
#                     clock and atmosphere at 0 of 8, so the
#                     coin sits in this rung's own air and not in the geometry. A rung edited until
#                     its baseline stops moving would be a rung selected on its own result
#   gradability, as one probe and NOT as a claim about the gate: `set pilot_emcon_frac 3.0` on the sweep
#                     (G5's `emcon-wide`) takes rung 01 from (20, 12)/(16, 8) to (22, 14)/(14, 6) with
#                     4 AIM-120 off the rail against 0 [MESS, rung 01]. The baseline sweep goes to radar
#                     STANDBY at t ~ 6 s under its own emission discipline and never re-radiates; that
#                     is the room the gene has, and it is reported, not removed.
#
# READING RULE, BINDING. THE EXIT CODE IS NOT THE VERDICT and no reader may quote it as one - every rung
# of this arena is a measuring rig and TIMEOUT (exit 3) is its normal end. THE MEASUREMENT IS THE PAIR
# (V, M) PER GRADED SIDE, computed the way doc/doctrine-evolution.md section 1 computes it: V is the sum
# of the judge's own `UNIT_RESULT` ranks over the side's aircraft (SUCCESS 3, TIMEOUT/NONE 2, FAIL 1,
# CRASH/LOC 0) and M is the number of that side's `mission OBJECTIVE ... state=met` lines. Read, in this
# order: (1) both `mission OBJECTIVE` blocks - if either side publishes none, the rung has lost property
# 3 and nothing else in the file is worth reading; (2) `stores DELIVERY aimErrM` against the 100.2 m
# soft fail radius; (3) `site LAUNCH ... brgDeg` - the belt has no IFF and WHO it shot at is a result;
# (4) the (V, M) pair. A reader who reports a kill count has read a warhead's arrival geometry.

net ar10net
  control ar10nod
  link wire
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free
  member ar10nod
  member ar10sam autonomy hold
  member ar10aaa autonomy hold

unit ar10str1
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight ar10st 1
  spawn 44.94000 0.00000 2500 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode off
  set attack_mode ccrp
  set rwr on
  set datalink on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  wp 44.94000 0.30000 2500 450
  wp 44.94000 0.00000 2500 450
  objective kill unit ar10ts1
  objective survive

